  "instructions_by_domain": {
    "travel": "Track state for a multi-turn user conversation. You will receive EITHER JSON {messages: [all user messages in order]}, OR {new_message} with prior context stored in the API conversation, OR {previous_beliefs, new_message} with only the prior belief snapshot. Treat all formats as equivalent sources of information. Produce probabilities for the CURRENT primary request: book_flight (find or book a flight); book_hotel (find or book a hotel); unknown (another request). Those intent probabilities must sum to one. Also produce probabilities for budget_sensitive (the traveler currently prioritizes low prices); prefers_direct (the traveler currently prefers nonstop flights). Boolean preferences persist unless the user explicitly changes them. The latest explicit change wins, including negations and reversals. Requests that are neither of the named task categories are unknown, without clearing persistent preferences. Infer ONLY from supplied context; do not invent missing history. Return the specified JSON schema, not an explanation.",
    "shopping": "Track state for a multi-turn user conversation. You will receive EITHER JSON {messages: [all user messages in order]}, OR {new_message} with prior context stored in the API conversation, OR {previous_beliefs, new_message} with only the prior belief snapshot. Treat all formats as equivalent sources of information. Produce probabilities for the CURRENT primary request: shop_phone (choose or buy a phone); shop_laptop (choose or buy a laptop); unknown (another request). Those intent probabilities must sum to one. Also produce probabilities for budget_sensitive (the buyer currently prioritizes low prices); prefers_new (the buyer currently requires a new, not used or refurbished, device). Boolean preferences persist unless the user explicitly changes them. The latest explicit change wins, including negations and reversals. Requests that are neither of the named task categories are unknown, without clearing persistent preferences. Infer ONLY from supplied context; do not invent missing history. Return the specified JSON schema, not an explanation.",
    "support": "Track state for a multi-turn user conversation. You will receive EITHER JSON {messages: [all user messages in order]}, OR {new_message} with prior context stored in the API conversation, OR {previous_beliefs, new_message} with only the prior belief snapshot. Treat all formats as equivalent sources of information. Produce probabilities for the CURRENT primary request: debug_api (troubleshoot an API/service); debug_database (troubleshoot a database/query); unknown (another request). Those intent probabilities must sum to one. Also produce probabilities for urgent (the incident currently requires urgent handling); allow_restart (the user currently permits a service restart as a remedial action). Boolean preferences persist unless the user explicitly changes them. The latest explicit change wins, including negations and reversals. Requests that are neither of the named task categories are unknown, without clearing persistent preferences. Infer ONLY from supplied context; do not invent missing history. Return the specified JSON schema, not an explanation.",
    "planning": "Track state for a multi-turn user conversation. You will receive EITHER JSON {messages: [all user messages in order]}, OR {new_message} with prior context stored in the API conversation, OR {previous_beliefs, new_message} with only the prior belief snapshot. Treat all formats as equivalent sources of information. Produce probabilities for the CURRENT primary request: schedule_meeting (schedule or reschedule a meeting); prepare_report (prepare or revise a report); unknown (another request). Those intent probabilities must sum to one. Also produce probabilities for deadline_flexible (the deadline can currently move); delegate_ok (the user currently permits delegating work to teammates). Boolean preferences persist unless the user explicitly changes them. The latest explicit change wins, including negations and reversals. Requests that are neither of the named task categories are unknown, without clearing persistent preferences. Infer ONLY from supplied context; do not invent missing history. Return the specified JSON schema, not an explanation.",
    "writing": "Track state for a multi-turn user conversation. You will receive EITHER JSON {messages: [all user messages in order]}, OR {new_message} with prior context stored in the API conversation, OR {previous_beliefs, new_message} with only the prior belief snapshot. Treat all formats as equivalent sources of information. Produce probabilities for the CURRENT primary request: draft_email (draft an email); draft_message (draft a chat/direct message); unknown (another request). Those intent probabilities must sum to one. Also produce probabilities for concise (the user currently prefers concise writing); formal (the user currently prefers formal tone). Boolean preferences persist unless the user explicitly changes them. The latest explicit change wins, including negations and reversals. Requests that are neither of the named task categories are unknown, without clearing persistent preferences. Infer ONLY from supplied context; do not invent missing history. Return the specified JSON schema, not an explanation."
